Description: Grow the output buffer past the requested length
 xo_buf_has_some_room rounds the size it needs up to a whole block. When
 that size was already a whole block, the buffer did not grow, and the
 room ended exactly at the requested length. xo_format_string_direct
 asks for one byte less than it writes for each XML or HTML entity, so it
 could write one byte past the heap buffer. It formats strings with a
 width and locale strings. With --libxo xml or html, w prints other
 users' command lines this way.
Origin: backport, https://github.com/Juniper/libxo/commit/4c9a0634e0785451f1ce394aebd099fed6df88b8
Author: Phil Shafer
Last-Update: 2026-11-17

--- a/libxo/xo_buf.h
+++ b/libxo/xo_buf.h
@@ -6,6 +6,9 @@
  * using the SOFTWARE, you agree to be bound by the terms of that
  * LICENSE.
  * Phil Shafer, August 2015
+ *
+ * Modified 2026-11-17: xo_buf_has_some_room leaves room past the requested
+ * length when it grows the buffer.
  */
 
 /*
@@ -154,7 +157,7 @@ xo_buf_has_some_room (xo_buffer_t *xbp,
 	 * Find out how much new space we need, round it up to bufsiz
 	 */
 	ssize_t sz = (xbp->xb_curp + len) - xbp->xb_bufp;
-	sz = (sz + bufsiz - 1) & ~(bufsiz - 1);
+	sz = (sz + bufsiz) & ~(bufsiz - 1);
 
 	char *bp = xo_realloc(xbp->xb_bufp, sz);
 	if (bp == NULL)
